-- Organization tag vocabulary (labels and groups in lib/booking/tag-catalog.ts).
comment on column organizations.tags is
  'Free tags, filterable in the booking sheet (Filters > tags). Groups: WHAT THEY ARE (auto from name/research): type-chamber-series, chamber-specialist, type-community-concerts, type-university, type-festival, type-arts-center, type-museum-church, size-large-stage. WHERE: nyc (automatic from city, trigger organizations_nyc_tag; write the city as "<City>, NY"; NYC venues get no fee pitch), nyc-under-5h (about 5 h or less by car from Midtown), tour-northwest / tour-midwest (2028-29 regional tours around Monmouth OR and Duluth MN). OUR MARKS (set by people): prestigious, priority-a / priority-b / priority-c (round 2 review Nov 2026), existing-relationship, josefina-2025. NOT A FIT: rental-only, closed, notfit-pop-broadway, notfit-orchestra-opera-dance, notfit-jazz-folk, notfit-specialist, notfit-education, exclude-booking-usa-cold-outreach (never in a mass first email). Bookkeeping (hidden in filters): research-claude / research-chatgpt (automatic from profile.researchedBy; do not add by hand), booking-usa-*, musical-america-*. Other lowercase tags are genres imported with lists. ChatGPT: when you research an organization, add the type-* tags that apply and, if it is not a fit, the notfit-* reason; never remove tags set by people.';
